 As a Data scientist, your missions will focus on making direct contributions to the development of new climate models or forecasting tools.










 Your key missions will include:



* Improving or developing new algorithms, new risk models and products for our B2B client;
* Identifying, implementing and deploying new statistical and machine learning methods to differentiate Descartes from its competitors;
* Participating in the development of Descartes’ technological platform;
* Collaborating with the business team to understand client needs and issues to further strengthen our technical excellence;
* Taking on management responsibilities as both you and the company develop;
* Working autonomously and pragmatically to make appropriate technical decisions.















**ABOUT YOU** 




***EXPERIENCE \& QUALIFICATIONS***



* Master’s student in data science, computer science, applied mathematics, statistics or meteorological studies or related;
* Ideally a previous experience (long\-term internship) in data science or climate modeling is valued.



***SKILLS***



* Proficient in statistics, applied mathematics and machine learning methods;
* Capable of building high\-performance algorithms;
* Proficiency in Python (e.g. scikit\-learn);
* Fluency in English (written and verbal communication) is required;
* Good command of one additional language (e.g. Chinese, French, Italian, German, Spanish...) is valued.



***MINDSET***



* Interested in weather and natural perils modeling (wildfires, hail, tsunamis, earthquakes etc);
* Excellent team player with an entrepreneurial mindset and value of diversity;
* Highly motivated, able to meet deadlines set;
* Strong desire to learn and commitment to the organization’s mission;
* Results oriented, high energy, with the ability to work in a dynamic and multi\-cultural environment;
* Eager to learn more about the insurance industry.















**WHY JOIN DESCARTES UNDERWRITING ?** 



* Opportunity to work and learn with teams from the most prestigious schools and research labs in the world, allowing you to progress towards technical excellence;
* Commitment from Descartes to its staff of continued learning and development (think annual seminars, training etc.);
* Work in a collaborative \& professional environment;
* Be part of a dynamic international team, passionate about diversity;
* Join a company with a true purpose – help us help our clients be more resilient towards climate risks;
* A competitive salary, bonus and benefits;
* You can benefit from punctual home office days.









*At Descartes Underwriting, we cherish the value of diversity whatever it may be. We are committed to fighting against all forms of discrimination and for equal opportunities. We foster an inclusive work environment that respects all differences.With equal skills, all our positions are open to people with disabilities.* 
















**RECRUITMENT PROCESS** 



* Step 1: HR Interview with our Talent Recruiter
* Step 2: Technical online test on Github
* Step 3: Remote technical interview with a Data Scientist
* Step 4: In\-person team interview to meet our Data Scientist team and discover our offices (could be held remotely if you are abroad)

The company is building the control layer for an energy\-constrained world — deploying AI, machine learning, and reinforcement learning to optimize HVAC systems, industrial equipment, and large\-scale energy loads across commercial buildings, factories, hospitals, and data centers. The focus is on real, measurable impact: autonomous control systems that drive 20–30%\+ energy savings in production environments.










 We're looking for a
 **BMS Control Engineer / Forward Deployment Engineer (TPM)** 
 who will join the team. This is a hands\-on role for someone who doesn't just design building automation systems, but has deployed, commissioned, and optimized them in real\-world infrastructure.










 This role is for someone who takes full ownership of field deployments — from site discovery to production rollout. You'll work at the intersection of BMS/BAS systems, HVAC controls, and AI\-driven optimization, deploying autonomous control systems across commercial buildings, factories, hospitals, and data centers.










**Your responsibilities will include:** 



* Own deployments end\-to\-end: site discovery, integration, commissioning, validation, and rollout;
* Install, configure, and commission BAS/BMS and PLC\-integrated systems;
* Deploy gateways, sensors, submeters, and communications infrastructure;
* Perform startup, point\-to\-point testing, and controls validation;
* Interface with AHUs, RTUs, chillers, boilers, pumps, cooling towers, and VFDs;
* Integrate through BACnet (IP \& MS/TP), Modbus, LON, and IP networks;
* Work with Niagara, Siemens, Honeywell, Johnson Controls Metasys, Delta, and other BAS platforms;
* Configure addressing, routing, communications, and device connectivity;
* Diagnose controls hardware, wiring, networking, protocol, and sensor issues;
* Support deployment of AI\-driven and RL\-driven control strategies;
* Own deployment schedules, communications, milestones, and execution;
* Coordinate customers, contractors, vendors, and internal engineering teams;
* Maintain deployment plans, commissioning reports, diagrams, and as\-built documentation.









**What we expect from you:** 



* Degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, HVAC, or related discipline — or equivalent BAS/PLC/SCADA/DCIM experience;
* 2\+ years of hands\-on BACnet experience (IP \& MS/TP);
* 2\+ years of Modbus experience;
* 2\+ years of HVAC Controls / DDC / BMS experience;
* Strong understanding of BMS/DDC systems, PLCs, PID loops, hydronics, and refrigeration;
* Experience with BAS platforms: Niagara (Tridium), Siemens, Honeywell, Johnson Controls Metasys, Delta;
* Hands\-on commissioning and troubleshooting experience in the field;
* Ability to work independently and take ownership in customer\-facing environments.









**Nice to have:** 



* Niagara (Tridium), EPA 608, NATE, or OSHA certifications;
* Experience in industrial facilities, healthcare, mission\-critical environments, or data centers;
* Exposure to IoT, edge computing, SCADA, or DCIM platforms;
* Experience with LON protocol and IP networking in BAS contexts.









**We offer:** 



* Full\-time engagement on a high\-impact infrastructure project;
* Remote\-friendly with on\-site deployment work at client facilities;
* Direct work with cutting\-edge AI and reinforcement learning applied to real\-world systems;
* Measurable impact — 20–30%\+ energy savings across live deployments;
* Opportunity to help define the future of autonomous building and industrial control systems.
